From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PRO 5 Recovery Bring-up <pro5-port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 03:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] defconfig: disable DECON LPD for recovery

Live recovery diagnostics show that the framebuffer and backlight stay active
while DECON enters LPD and DSIM is runtime-suspended.  A page-zero PAN wakes
DECON and updates VSYNC, but the display returns to LPD about 70 milliseconds
later.  Keep the recovery display pipeline active instead of allowing the
normal Android low-power display policy to shut it down between redraws.
---
 arch/arm64/configs/cm_pro5_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/cm_pro5_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/cm_pro5_defconfig
index a2fcae38..a3a331d2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/cm_pro5_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/cm_pro5_defconfig
@@ -2291,7 +2291,7 @@
 CONFIG_EXYNOS_DECON=y
 CONFIG_EXYNOS_DECON_FB=y
 CONFIG_EXYNOS_DECON_DPU=y
-CONFIG_DECON_LPD_DISPLAY=y
+# CONFIG_DECON_LPD_DISPLAY is not set
 CONFIG_DECON_BLOCKING_MODE=y
 CONFIG_DECON_EVENT_LOG=y
 # CONFIG_DECON_DISPLAY_LOGO is not set
-- 
2.39.5
